# Embed System Architecture

## End-to-End Pipeline

### Scraping Phase (scripts/news-scraper.js)
1. Firecrawl scrapes article → returns `markdown`, `html`, `rawHtml`
2. **Stage 1**: `extractAllEmbedsFromMarkdown(content)` — converts markdown links to tokens
3. **Stage 2**: `htmlToTokens(rawHtml)` — uses cheerio to find embeds in HTML
4. **Stage 3**: `replaceTikTokBlockquote()` / `replaceTwitterBlockquote()` — swaps blockquotes with tokens
5. Line-by-line cleanup removes social media UI garbage text
6. Content (with tokens) sent to Groq LLM for Turkish→English translation
7. Translated content saved to Supabase `tech_news_articles.content`

### Rendering Phase (frontend)
1. `SmartMarkdown.tsx` receives content from Supabase
2. `GLOBAL_TOKEN_REGEX` extracts `[[EMBED:TYPE:DATA]]` tokens
3. Content split into markdown parts + embed parts
4. Embed parts → `EmbedFromToken` → routes to platform-specific component
5. Fallback: `EmbedFromURL` handles legacy content (plain URLs in paragraphs)

## Token Format Specification

| Platform | Token Format | Data |
|----------|-------------|------|
| YouTube  | `[[EMBED:YOUTUBE:VIDEO_ID]]` | 11-char video ID (e.g. `dQw4w9WgXcQ`) |
| Twitter  | `[[EMBED:TWEET:TWEET_ID]]` | Numeric tweet ID (e.g. `1876543212345678901`) |
| TikTok   | `[[EMBED:TIKTOK:FULL_URL]]` | Full URL (e.g. `https://www.tiktok.com/@user/video/123`) |

Frontend regex: `/\[\[EMBED:(TIKTOK|TWEET|YOUTUBE):([^\]]+)\]\]/g`

